  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Deelname KCC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project supports the meaningful and sustained participation of young volunteers from the Jonge Klimaatbeweging (Youth Climate Movement) in the Klimaatcrisis Coalitie (KCC) in the Netherlands over the course of one year (August 2025 &#x2013; July 2026).Through this grant, Jonge Klimaatbeweging will be able to cover essential costs such as transportation, food, and accessibility support, enablingdiverse youth voices to actively contribute to KCC meetings, campaigns, and advocacy moments. The initiative ensures that financialbarriers do not exclude young people from decision-making spaces where climate justice is discussed and shaped.The volunteers represent the voice of over 100,000 youth across the Netherlands and bring a fresh, intergenerational and justice-centered perspective tothe coalition&#x2019;s work. Their presence strengthens the coalition&apos;s legitimacy and its ability to develop inclusive strategies on climate policy and mobilization.By the end of the grant period, Jonge Klimaatbeweging aims to have enhanced youth participation in the national climate movement, created leadership opportunities for young volunteers, and contributed meaningfully to the collective actions and narratives of the KCC. The project also hopes to generate learnings on how to structurally embed youth participation within broad-based climate coalitions.</narrative>
  </description>
